NAME
       which - show the full path of a command

SYNOPSIS
       which COMMAND...

DESCRIPTION
       which searches the directories in $PATH, in order, and prints the path
       of the program that would run for each COMMAND, such as
       /usr/sbin/useradd. On RHEL 9 it also shows aliases. When a command is
       not found it prints which directories it searched and exits with 1.

       The shell's own builtins (cd, echo) are not programs; ask bash with
       type COMMAND to see how the shell will treat a name.

EXAMPLES
           which useradd
           rpm -qf $(which ss)

SEE ALSO
       type (in builtins(1)), whereis(1), bash(1)
